import java.util.* ;
import java.io.*; 
import java.util.ArrayList;

public class Solution {

	public static ArrayList<Integer> rowWaveForm(ArrayList<ArrayList<Integer>> mat) {
     ArrayList<Integer> res = new ArrayList<>();
        int n = mat.size();
		int m = mat.get(0).size();

		for(int i = 0 ; i < n;i++){
			if(i % 2  == 0){
				for(int j = 0 ; j < m;j++){
					res.add(mat.get(i).get(j));
				}
			}else{
				for(int j = m-1 ; j >= 0; j--){
					res.add(mat.get(i).get(j));
				}
			}
		}
				return res;
			}
		}
You are given a 2D array with dimensions ‘N*M’. You need to read the array elements row-wise and return a 
linear array that stores the elements like a wave i.e the 1st-row elements are stored from left to right, 2nd-row elements are
stored from right to left, and so on.

For test case 1, the array is traversed as:
The first row is traversed from left to right. -> [1, 2]
The second row is traversed from right to left. -> [5, 0]
Therefore the final answer is [1, 2, 5, 0].
